<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hari Om Sharan's recording</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1974</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording on traditional melodies, re-released 1995</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hariharan and Gulshan Kumar's recording</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1992</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording; first devotional song to pass 5 billion YouTube views (2025)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Mahaviri commentary (Rambhadracharya)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1983</span><span class="sg-chain-h">commentary</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Shri Hanuman Chalisa album (Amitabh Bachchan and twenty singers)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2011</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">1920 (Vikram Bhatt)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recited in the film</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Bajrangi Bhaijaan</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used in a key sequence</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Shri Hanuman Chalisa, animated film (Charuvi Agarwal)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">animated film</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ben Raivitz's version</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2026</span><span class="sg-chain-h">tribute to Smit Machchhar</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ramayana</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Hanuman's deeds in Rama's service are its subject</span></li></ul></section>
